Goldenland AI Assist workflow (USER PREFERENCE — missing it gets called out): per implement ticket, load the originating issue via gh and read its 'Parent' section + acceptance criteria first. Two-axis code review (standards + spec) via parallel delegate/reviewer sub-agents is mandatory before commit; they inherit the session model and have shell access in the repo cwd, and there is no specialized code-review subagent — pass explicit shell diff instructions (`git diff <fixed-point>...HEAD`, `git log <fixed-point>..HEAD`). The code-review skill needs an explicit fixed point (SHA/tag/branch/range) — if none given, pin it per-ticket from the commit graph (feature commit's parent SHA). Ledger to docs/agents/reviews/<issue>.md: fixed point, spec source, standards sources, findings table (finding/axis/classification/disposition). Before writing ledgers, verify findings against HEAD — later batch tickets may already fix them (e.g. #17/#18); distinguish resolved-by-later-commit vs still-open-at-HEAD before assigning dispositions. Delete dead code only when it has zero references at HEAD, excluding .pi-subagents/ and docs/agents/reviews/. Never skip the Resolve step: `gh issue close` with summary (commit SHA, test results, ledger path), appending a context-pointer comment (not a separate file) to #1's 'Implementation Decisions'. Batched close-outs: run 2 axes × N tickets as parallel sub-agents (unlimited spawn budget); trust nothing from workflow completion events (truncated aggregates, transient 'Model is unavailable' child failures) — inspect raw outputs in .pi-subagents/artifacts/ and re-run failed children. Testing: when a fix changes behavior, update existing tests that encoded the old (buggy) contract (e.g. GA4 health tests needed ga4_key_events added after gating health on key events); regression tests for fixed bugs go alongside existing tests (DomainBlacklistServiceTest, Ga4HealthTest). <!-- created=2026-08-08, last=2026-08-08 -->